(3.2) Determine what I can buy from the list below spending exactly 150 e,
given that I want to buy at least one piece per each article:
- T-shirt e 15.10;
- pair of socks e 15.30;
- hat e 9.50;
- shorts e 29.60;
- pair of gloves e17.50.

(1.4) Say which one among the following statements applies to the Skolemi-
zation procedure:
(a) it produces an equi-satisﬁable formula in the same language;
(b) it produces an equi-satisﬁable formula in a larger language;
(c) it produces an equi-satisﬁable formula in a restricted language;
(d) it produces an equi-satisﬁable open formula.
Part II: Exercises to be solved manually.

(1.4) Congruence Closure decides the satisﬁability of:
(a) a ﬁnite set of sentences in prenex normal form;
(b) a ﬁnite set of universal sentences;
(c) a ﬁnite set of arbitrary formulae;
(d) a ﬁnite set of literals.
Part II: Exercises to be solved manually.

(1.3) Which one of the following statements is correct?
2 congruence closure is a decision procedure for satisfiability of sentences
in difference logic;
2 congruence closure is a decision procedure for satisfiability of ground
literals in EUF;
2 congruence closure is a decision procedure for satisfiability of first order
sentences;
2 congruence closure is a decision procedure for satisfiability of a finite
sets of propositional sentences.

(1.3) Which one of the following statements is correct?
2 structural transformations convert a propositional formula into CNF
up to logical equivalence;
2 structural transformations convert a formula into DNF up to logical
equivalence;
2 structural transformations employ the distributivity law to ensure effi-
ciency in the CNF-conversion;
2 structural transformations cannot convert a satisfiable formula into an
unsatisfiable one.

(1.3) Which ones of the following theories are convex?
2 linear real arithmetic;
2 linear integer arithmetic;
2 EUF;
2 the theory of arrays.
